# Beliefs equivalent for one goal, different for another

Generated by `equiv.py` (exploratory). Pairs of test decisions at the same step with the same optimal set and horizon-free QMDP values (Σ_s b(s) γ^d), in centred effective steps (log_γ), within 0.5 step under goal A, goal A worth ≥ 0.4 to both beliefs, and disjoint optimal sets at least 1.0 step apart under goal B, pooled over ordered goal pairs: 5349 (4919–6000) pairs per model (largest difference of effective steps under A 0.30 (0.27–0.32), under B 1.52 (1.48–1.59); posteriors 1.94 (1.93–1.96) apart in L1). The model's own decision is the same for the two beliefs under A in 0.60 (0.49–0.68) and under B in 0.39 (0.30–0.39). Medians (min–max) over six models.

